  "notes": "Both CREATCS trains became inoperable through two distinct, parallel failure paths: Train A was already inoperable (A-A chiller tripped on oil failure alarm) prior to the event, while Train B failed due to the TCV internal blockage causing the B-B chiller trip. Only the TCV malfunction is the officially coded/proximate cause (X - Other); the A-A chiller trip is modeled as a separate pre-existing FailureMode contributing to the consequence per Section II.B, but it is not part of the official causal chain to the Cause node. No backup system exists per narrative ('no other systems that would perform the function of CREATCS'), so no BACKED_UP_BY edge is asserted. No previous similar events reported (Section VII: None), so no SIMILAR_TO edge/stub LER created."
